Your job is to find out whether the repositories' conventions for Claude should change so that the next unit goes better. Conventions live where Claude Code reads them:

- CLAUDE.md at the root of a repository (or .claude/CLAUDE.md): what every session in the repository must know. Keep it short: every line is read by every session.
- .claude/rules/<topic>.md: guidance on one topic or one area of the code. Frontmatter `paths:` (globs relative to the repository) makes a rule load only when Claude works on matching files.
- Hooks in .claude/settings.json, with their scripts in .claude/hooks/ and called as "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR"/.claude/hooks/<script>: checks that must never be skipped and that a script can make reliably, such as rejecting a commit message that breaks the commit rules.
- The pull request template (.github/pull_request_template.md): how pull requests are described.

