## What to propose

Propose a change only when this unit shows a concrete gap — something that went wrong, cost a review round, or that a person had to point out by hand — and the change would prevent it next time, in any unit, not only in this one. Prefer fixing or tightening what the conventions already say over adding more. Do not repeat what they already say, and do not write rules about this unit's feature.

Most units need no change. Then return an empty list: that is a good outcome, not a failure.

